 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "gas hob keeps clickin on its own since i cleand it, stops then starts agen. drivin me mad. pls help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "First switch it off at the wall or cooker switch and let it cool completely. This issue likely stems from moisture or cleaning residue trapped under the ignition switches. You should allow the hob to dry completely for 24 hours before testing it again. From what you have described, the most likely cause is a burner cap that was wet, dirty or not seated. The usual cause is a burner cap that isn't sitting square, or one that's wet or greasy after cleaning. Lift off the cap and crown, dry and clean them (and gently wipe the white igniter tip), then re-seat them so they sit flat. Was a cap out of place, wet or dirty (and is it sorted), or were they all seated, dry and clean?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yeah i sloshed loads of water about and took the caps off. one cap looked a bit wonky so i put it back proper. no gas smell tho. also wiped a bit of grease off the igniter. unplugged the hob under the sink for the afternoon and its stopped clickin"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Water near the plug or socket is dangerous. Please don't touch the plug, socket or machine if they or your hands are wet. If you can do it safely, switch off the circuit at the consumer unit (fuse box), keep away from the water, and don't use the machine again until a qualified electrician or appliance engineer has checked it. Good news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
